# Fixture 03 — ID formats (A1). Captured 2026-08-15 ~05:40Z, live api.agentmail.to.
# Throwaway pod 9047724b-2879-416b-8424-82ef81ab9397, inbox amk-probe@agentmail.to.

## organization_id / pod_id / inbox_id (from create responses)
organization_id : 133c9cbe-f996-4094-a8d5-0c6603e022ea   (UUID v4)
pod_id          : 9047724b-2879-416b-8424-82ef81ab9397   (UUID v4)
inbox_id        : amk-probe@agentmail.to                 (== email address, used verbatim as path param)

## thread_id
thread_id       : c1197a89-02ad-4bdf-8461-c03136b481aa   (UUID v4)

## message_id — THE KEY FINDING
POST /v0/inboxes/amk-probe@agentmail.to/messages/send  ->  SendMessageResponse:
{"message_id":"<010001a003ef6970-1732f5b7-5c17-485b-92fa-52ccd78a0004-000000@email.amazonses.com>","thread_id":"c1197a89-02ad-4bdf-8461-c03136b481aa"}

- message_id is an RFC 5322 angle-bracket Message-ID: <local-part@email.amazonses.com>
- It is the AWS SES OUTBOUND Message-ID (@email.amazonses.com) — i.e. HEADER-DERIVED
  from the SES send, NOT minted by AgentMail. Inbound mail will carry the sender's
  own Message-ID (to be confirmed with a swaks inbound; see 09-*).
- Contains '<', '>', and '@' — all must be percent-encoded in a path segment:
  path form: %3C010001a003ef6970-1732f5b7-5c17-485b-92fa-52ccd78a0004-000000%40email.amazonses.com%3E
  round-trip GET /messages/<enc>/raw returned 200 with the decoded id echoed. CONFIRMED.

## Extra response fields NOT in the Fern SDK types (SDK parses with passthrough)
On MessageItem in a list response, live API additionally returns:
  organization_id, pod_id, smtp_id
e.g. "smtp_id":"rubgu1m5dvksbo540fukt0e60jvj5oelrltfobjm"  (SES-side id, also used in the CDN raw path)
=> amk MessageItem must EMIT organization_id + pod_id + smtp_id for a clean conformance diff,
   even though the SDK does not type them.

## Pagination boundary (A1/A4 partial)
GET /messages?limit=1 with exactly 1 message in the inbox -> response has NO next_page_token
(count:1, limit:1, messages:[...]).  => token is ABSENT on the last page, not empty-string.
Full multi-page token shape still needs >=2 messages; see 04-pagination.http.

## Raw list envelope (verbatim, limit=1)
{"count":1,"limit":1,"messages":[{"organization_id":"133c9cbe-...","pod_id":"9047724b-...",
"inbox_id":"amk-probe@agentmail.to","thread_id":"c1197a89-...","message_id":"<...@email.amazonses.com>",
"labels":["sent"],"timestamp":"2026-08-15T05:40:16.825Z","from":"AMK Probe <amk-probe@agentmail.to>",
"to":["amk-probe@agentmail.to"],"subject":"AMK probe A1 baseline",
"preview":"probe body for id-format capture\n\n--\nSent via AgentMail",
"smtp_id":"rubgu1m5dvksbo540fukt0e60jvj5oelrltfobjm","size":1269,
"updated_at":"...","created_at":"..."}]}

Note: a self-send (to == from == inbox) is stored labeled ["sent"] only (no separate
received copy observed in-inbox). A genuine message.received requires external inbound.
